.TH std::inplace_vector::pop_back 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::inplace_vector::pop_back \- std::inplace_vector::pop_back

.SH Synopsis
constexpr void pop_back();

Removes the last element of the container.

Calling pop_back on an empty container results in undefined behavior.

Iterators and references to the last element are invalidated. The end() iterator is also
invalidated.

.SH Parameters

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Return value

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Complexity

Constant.

.SH Exceptions

Throws nothing.

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <inplace_vector>
#include <print>

int main()
{
    std::inplace_vector<int, 4> numbers{1, 2, 3};
    for (; not numbers.empty(); numbers.pop_back())
        std::println("{}", numbers);
}

.SH Output:

[1, 2, 3]
[1, 2]
[1]

.SH See also

push_back adds an element to the end
          \fI(public member function)\fP
